("Library induction","Section 2",
 "Welcome, everyone, to your library induction. I'll be quick, because I know you want to start exploring. The ground floor is for group work, and talking is fine there. The first floor is a quiet zone, so please keep your voices low. On the second floor you will find silent study rooms, which you can book online for up to three hours. The books are arranged by subject number, not by author, so ask at the desk if you cannot find something. You may borrow ten books at a time for four weeks. If you keep a book longer, the fine is fifty pence a day. Printing is on the ground floor, and you need to add credit to your card first. Finally, the library closes at midnight during exams, but it is only open until eight in the evening on Sundays.",
 [("Where is talking allowed?",["Ground floor","First floor","Second floor","Nowhere"],0),
  ("How long can a study room be booked for?",["One hour","Two hours","Three hours","All day"],2),
  ("How are the books arranged?",["By author","By subject number","By colour","By date"],1),
  ("What is the fine for a late book?",["Fifty pence a day","One pound a day","Five pounds a week","There is no fine"],0),
  ("When does the library close on Sundays?",["Midnight","Eight in the evening","Six in the evening","It is closed"],1)]),
